    "note": "USB adapter that turns the F-16 Cougar TQS into its own USB game controller (Windows numbers the buttons 1-32; BMS .key files count from 0). Buttons from the TUSBA user guide (firmware v1.07): DX1-13 the Cougar switches and the centre positions of COMMS, DOGFIGHT and SPEED BRAKE (centre buttons can be disabled), DX14-16 throttle areas Idle / Mil / Afterburner, DX17-32 user-configured buttons linked to analog values (disabled by default). Analog axes: throttle, cursor X/Y, range, antenna elevation plus 3 derived throttle axes (Idle, Mil, AB); their DirectInput axis names are not documented. VID:PID and product string not published. The DOGFIGHT outboard/inboard and COMMS directions follow the guide's names, not verified on hardware."
